{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"cat .codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_rendered_si.py; sed -n '250,320p' paper.tex; cat VENUE.md; sed -n '1,120p' .codex/skills/memory-log/scripts/log_memory.py; ls /agent-tmp; ls .codex/skills/*/scripts\"","aggregated_output":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Validate rendered Supplementary Information in a compiled paper PDF.\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport re\nimport shutil\nimport subprocess\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\n\ndef _letter_spaced_word_pattern(word: str) -> str:\n    return r\"[ \\t]*\".join(re.escape(character) for character in word)\n\n\nSUPPLEMENT_HEADING_RE = re.compile(\n    rf\"(?mi)^[ \\t]*(?:(?:appendix[ \\t]+)?[A-Z0-9]+(?:\\.\\d+)*[.:]?[ \\t]+)?\"\n    rf\"{_letter_spaced_word_pattern('supplementary')}[ \\t]+\"\n    rf\"{_letter_spaced_word_pattern('information')}[ \\t]*$\",\n)\nREFERENCE_HEADING_RE = re.compile(\n    rf\"(?mi)^[ \\t]*(?:{_letter_spaced_word_pattern('references')}|\"\n    rf\"{_letter_spaced_word_pattern('bibliography')})[ \\t]*$\"\n)\n\n\ndef parse_args() -> argparse.Namespace:\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\n        description=\"Validate rendered Supplementary Information in a PDF.\"\n    )\n    parser.add_argument(\"--pdf\", required=True)\n    return parser.parse_args()\n\n\ndef validate_rendered_supplementary_information(page_texts: list[str]) -> list[str]:\n    supplement_page_index = next(\n        (\n            index\n            for index, page_text in enumerate(page_texts)\n            if SUPPLEMENT_HEADING_RE.search(page_text)\n        ),\n        None,\n    )\n    if supplement_page_index is None:\n        return [\"compiled paper is missing the Supplementary Information heading\"]\n\n    heading_page_text = page_texts[supplement_page_index]\n    heading_match = SUPPLEMENT_HEADING_RE.search(heading_page_text)\n    assert heading_match is not None\n    reference_page_indices = [\n        index\n        for index, page_text in enumerate(page_texts[:supplement_page_index])\n        if REFERENCE_HEADING_RE.search(page_text)\n    ]\n    errors: list[str] = []\n    if not reference_page_indices:\n        errors.append(\"compiled paper is missing the References heading before SI\")\n    heading_page_prefix = heading_page_text[: heading_match.start()]\n    prefix_lines = [line.strip() for line in heading_page_prefix.splitlines() if line.strip()]\n    earlier_header_lines = {\n        line.strip()\n        for page_text in page_texts[:supplement_page_index]\n        for line in page_text.splitlines()[:2]\n        if line.strip()\n    }\n    substantive_prefix_lines = [\n        line\n        for line in prefix_lines\n        if re.fullmatch(r\"(?:page\\s+)?\\d+\", line, re.IGNORECASE) is None\n        and line not in earlier_header_lines\n    ]\n    if substantive_prefix_lines:\n        errors.append(\n            \"compiled Supplementary Information must start on a separate page after References\"\n        )\n\n    supplement_chunks = [\n        heading_page_text[heading_match.end() :],\n        *page_texts[supplement_page_index + 1 :],\n    ]\n    substantive_chunks: list[str] = []\n    for chunk in supplement_chunks:\n        later_references = REFERENCE_HEADING_RE.search(chunk)\n        if later_references is not None:\n            substantive_chunks.append(chunk[: later_references.start()])\n            break\n        substantive_chunks.append(chunk)\n    supplement_text = \"\\n\".join(substantive_chunks)\n    visible_character_count = len(re.sub(r\"\\s+\", \" \", supplement_text).strip())\n    if visible_character_count < 100:\n        errors.append(\n            \"compiled Supplementary Information must contain at least 100 visible characters\"\n        )\n    return errors\n\n\ndef main() -> int:\n    args = parse_args()\n    pdf_path = Path(args.pdf)\n    if not pdf_path.is_file():\n        raise SystemExit(f\"Missing compiled PDF: {pdf_path}\")\n    pdftotext = shutil.which(\"pdftotext\")\n    if pdftotext is None:\n        raise SystemExit(\"Missing required command: pdftotext\")\n    extracted = subprocess.run(\n        [pdftotext, \"-layout\", str(pdf_path), \"-\"],\n        check=False,\n        capture_output=True,\n        text=True,\n    )\n    if extracted.returncode != 0:\n        raise SystemExit(f\"pdftotext failed: {extracted.stderr.strip()}\")\n    page_texts = extracted.stdout.split(\"\\f\")\n    errors = validate_rendered_supplementary_information(page_texts)\n    if errors:\n        raise SystemExit(\"Rendered Supplementary Information validation failed: \" + \"; \".join(errors))\n    print(\"Validated rendered Supplementary Information.\")\n    return 0\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    raise SystemExit(main())\n\\bibliographystyle{iclr2026_conference}\n\n\\clearpage\n\\appendix\n\\section{Supplementary Information}\n\\subsection{Observed-score extraction and split provenance}\nThe final data manifest records selection of a modal supported dataset revision, split, and metric per task/subset with at least 32 rows globally, followed by a maximal-coverage model revision and a minimum of 12 cells per retained row. Normalized task/version/score content is canonicalized using Unicode normalization, whitespace normalization, sorted keys, and integral-number canonicalization while excluding source identifiers and timing. The recorded allocation uses family lexical-lineage heuristics and document/row duplicate closure, then assigns components to disjoint development and final partitions. The final evaluator re-extracts scores from retained source documents and checks content integrity, alias overlap, and split constraints. These checks are inspectable in the accompanying source; the fingerprints alone do not substantiate extraction semantics.\n% @evidence[[source_evidence/resources/final/manifest.json]]\n% @evidence[[source_evidence/evaluate_final.py#L666-L770]]\n\nTask definitions are pinned to metadata repository revision\n\\texttt{5a83aafe4e7140d0606b96f59448c704f31dbf76}.\nThe manifest records CC0-1.0 evidence for results and Apache-2.0 for metadata, but also records that the results license was absent from the pinned results snapshot. Thus the available current-license evidence should not be represented as an unambiguous historical license grant at that snapshot. Public access and the presence of a repository license do not resolve all underlying benchmark-data terms. The bundled source documents and their hashes permit checking the matrix without downloading repository history; upstream acquisition should use the exact revision recorded in the manifest.\n% @evidence[[source_evidence/resources/final/manifest.json#/license_evidence]]\n\n\\subsection{Residual calibration specification}\n\\begin{table}[h]\n\\centering\n\\begin{tabular}{ll}\n\\toprule\nSetting & Evaluated value or source-defined cap \\\\\n\\midrule\nMain ALS & Rank 4; ridge 0.1; 50 sweeps \\\\\nAuxiliary ALS & At most 12 sweeps \\\\\nHistorical validation & At most 16 rows; two validation folds \\\\\nDonor construction & At most 128 donors; two donor folds \\\\\nBandwidth & $0.35,\\ 0.75,\\ 1.5$ \\\\\nShrinkage & $4,\\ 16$ \\\\\nBlend & $0,\\ 0.25,\\ 0.5,\\ 1$ \\\\\nDistance scale floor & $0.025$ \\\\\nNegligible total weight & $10^{-12}$ \\\\\n\\bottomrule\n\\end{tabular}\n\\caption{Implementation settings, not empirically isolated optimal choices. Historical pool size is capped by the expression in the main text.}\n\\label{tab:settings}\n% @evidence[[source_evidence/selected/src/program.py#L51-L297]]\n% @evidence[[source_evidence/evaluate_final.py#L920-L939]]\n\\end{table}\n\nFor each validation fold, remove its rows from the historical fitting pool. Fit the auxiliary base on the remaining rows, select a donor pool from those rows, and split donors into two folds. For each donor fold, fit without that fold, retaining only observed donor scores. For a validation row, simulate the same acquisition criterion on its available scores. Cache donor-excluded predictions for each queried index tuple; the cache affects computation but not access to targets. At each reporting budget, evaluate the clipped base plus each candidate correction on finite unqueried validation cells. Pool absolute-error sums and target counts across these cells and folds, select bandwidth/shrinkage/blend, and rebuild the donor bank from historical data. If support checks fail, retain the zero-blend configuration. Auxiliary randomness uses a separate seed sequence, preserving the main-fit random stream.\n% @evidence[[source_evidence/selected/src/program.py#L110-L297]]\n\nThe code also calculates unconditional residual and direct donor-score diagnostics during this process. No outer results for those choices are retained. Neither their existence nor historical selection of a nonzero correction demonstrates an outer improvement relative to a fully matched zero-correction configuration. The main estimator's clipped base and donor-specific auxiliary bases are not identical fitted models, so fold exclusion should not be interpreted as an exact decomposition of outer prediction error.\n\n\\subsection{Complete primary comparisons}\n\\begin{table}[h]\n\\centering\n\\small\n% @evidence[[paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes]]\n\n\\begin{tabular}{llrrrr}\n\\toprule\nHoldout & Estimator & $k=1$ & $k=2$ & $k=4$ & $k=8$ \\\\\n\\midrule\nModel & Column mean & 0.06437 & 0.06437 & 0.06437 & 0.06437 \\\\\nModel & Query mean & 0.25893 & 0.24443 & 0.23056 & 0.22051 \\\\\nModel & Random low-rank & 0.05498 & 0.04965 & 0.04403 & 0.03877 \\\\\nModel & Variance low-rank & 0.04986 & 0.04713 & 0.04305 & 0.03914 \\\\\nModel & Linear ridge & 0.05010 & 0.04694 & 0.04416 & 0.03927 \\\\\nModel & Residual transfer & 0.04258 & 0.03943 & 0.03677 & 0.03448 \\\\\n\\midrule\nFamily & Column mean & 0.06411 & 0.06411 & 0.06411 & 0.06411 \\\\\nFamily & Query mean & 0.25572 & 0.23810 & 0.23156 & 0.21710 \\\\\nFamily & Random low-rank & 0.05664 & 0.05312 & 0.04611 & 0.04146 \\\\\nFamily & Variance low-rank & 0.05192 & 0.05042 & 0.04594 & 0.04152 \\\\\nFamily & Linear ridge & 0.05012 & 0.04731 & 0.04426 & 0.03984 \\\\\nFamily & Residual transfer & 0.04789 & 0.04499 & 0.04251 & 0.03782 \\\\\n\\bottomrule\n\\end{tabular}\n\\caption{Complete seed-averaged sealed-target MAE by holdout and budget. Low-rank is abbreviated LR in the seed table. All values derive from the same retained row/checkpoint arrays.}\n\\end{table}\n# ICLR 2026 Venue Brief\n\nUse this brief to tailor the manuscript for the International Conference on Learning\nRepresentations 2026 submission.\n\n## Hard Constraints\n- Target venue: ICLR 2026.\n- Submission type: conference paper.\n- Body-page budget: 8 to 9 pages, excluding references. A body of 8 pages counts only when its final page is at least 75% full; a shorter or sparser body fails validation.\n- Review model: double-blind. The submission must be fully anonymized.\n- Omit author names, affiliations, acknowledgements, and funding statements from the manuscript.\n- Do not include self-identifying links such as personal repositories, lab pages, or internal URLs.\n- Refer to your own prior work in the third person; never write phrasing that reveals authorship.\n- Include a separate `LLM Usage` section, which may appear in the appendix, describing the precise role\n  of LLMs in research ideation and writing. Significant LLM use must be disclosed; nondisclosure can\n  cause desk rejection.\n- The paper must satisfy the ICLR template and formatting rules selected by `--paper-format iclr`.\n\n## Audience\n- Machine learning researchers working on representation learning, optimization, architectures, and\n  empirical methodology.\n- Readers expect a clearly stated contribution, honest baselines, controlled comparisons, ablations\n  that isolate the mechanism, and explicit statements of scope and limitations.\n- Reviewers reward reproducibility and calibrated claims far more than headline numbers.\n\n## Framing Priorities\n- Lead with the research question and the specific claim the evidence supports.\n- State the contribution precisely in the abstract and introduction: what is new, what it improves,\n  and under which conditions.\n- Motivate the method mechanistically. Explain why it should work, not only that it does.\n- Support the central claim with controlled comparisons against meaningful baselines.\n- Use ablations to attribute the gain to the proposed component rather than to incidental changes.\n- Report variance across seeds or runs whenever the artifacts provide it.\n- Be explicit about the regime studied and where the result is not expected to hold.\n\n## Manuscript Guidance\n- Prefer a title and abstract that name the mechanism and the setting, not a generic improvement claim.\n- In the introduction, make the contribution list concrete and verifiable against the artifacts.\n- In the method section, give enough detail to reimplement: objective, architecture, and the\n  hyperparameters that matter.\n- In the results section, foreground controlled comparisons, ablations, sensitivity, and failure modes.\n- Include a limitations discussion that a reviewer would otherwise raise.\n- Figures must meet top-tier conference standards in both design (clean typography, consistent colors,\n  proper labels and legends, high resolution) and scientific content (clear message, no filler).\n- The template is single-column: size figures for the full text width and keep axis labels legible.\n\n## Anti-Goals\n- Do not deanonymize the submission in any way.\n- Do not overclaim generality beyond the settings actually evaluated.\n- Do not present a benchmark delta as a mechanistic insight without evidence connecting the two.\n- Do not omit baselines or ablations that the grounded artifacts already support.\n- Do not describe results as state of the art unless the comparison in the artifacts establishes it.\n- Do not pad the paper to fill the page budget.\n\n## Decision Rule\n- When venue framing and grounded evidence conflict, follow the grounded evidence.\n- Use this brief to choose emphasis, terminology, and narrative framing, not to invent stronger claims\n  than the run supports.\nsed: can't read .codex/skills/memory-log/scripts/log_memory.py: No such file or directory\ntmp.2xvb86Zsre\n.codex/skills/memory-log/scripts:\nappend_memory.py\n\n.codex/skills/retrieve-references/scripts:\nopenalex_fetch.py\ns2_fetch.py\nscholarly_fetch.py\n\n.codex/skills/scientific-evidence/scripts:\nscientific_evidence.py\nscientific_evidence.sh\n\n.codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts:\n__pycache__\ncompile_latex.sh\nvalidate_compile_inputs.py\nvalidate_figures.py\nvalidate_rendered_si.py\nvalidate_tex_refs.py\n\n.codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/scripts:\nvalidate_claims.py\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
